adjudication.rationale:
In sharing mode (`APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED` && `CALCOM_CREDENTIAL_SYNC_ENDPOINT`), `parseRefreshTokenResponse()` intentionally parses with `minimumTokenResponseSchema` and then *forces* a `refresh_token` field to the literal string "refresh_token" when the response lacks it:

```ts
if (!refreshTokenResponse.data.refresh_token) {
  refreshTokenResponse.data.refresh_token = "refresh_token";
}
```

Call sites (e.g. Zoom: `parsedToken = parseRefreshTokenResponse(responseBody, zoomRefreshedTokenSchema)`) treat the result like a normal `safeParse` output, so any existing logic that persists `parsedToken.data` (or merges it over existing credentials) will overwrite the real stored refresh token with this placeholder. This is directly verifiable in the diff for Office365, which merges the parsed data into the existing credential object before persisting:

```ts
o365AuthCredentials = { ...o365AuthCredentials, ...(tokenResponse.success && tokenResponse.data) };
await prisma.credential.update({ data: { key: o365AuthCredentials } });
```

So the core issue in the finding (placeholder refresh_token can replace the real one and break subsequent non-sharing refresh flows) is a real defect introduced by this change; the Zoom-specific persistence path isn’t shown in this diff, but the same pattern is now used there as well.
